# Smoking & Posture Detection

Real-time, multi-person video analysis that, for every tracked person, reports
both:

- a **posture** label — `STANDING` / `SITTING` / `WALKING` (from body geometry,
  independent of the action model), and
- a confirmed **smoking** state, raised only when several independent signals
  agree over time, which keeps false positives low in crowded or noisy scenes.

## How it works

The pipeline runs per frame and per tracked person:

1. **Person detection** – `yolov8n.pt` (Ultralytics YOLOv8) detects people and
   a lightweight IoU + center-distance tracker assigns stable track IDs.
2. **Pose estimation** – `yolov8n-pose.pt` extracts 17 COCO keypoints per
   person; keypoints are normalized into a 34-value vector per frame.
3. **Temporal action recognition** – a **CNN + BiLSTM** Keras model
   (`action_model.keras`) classifies a 30-frame window of pose + velocity +
   acceleration features (102 features/frame) into `smoke`, `sit`, `stand`,
   `walk`. See [`train_action_model.py`](train_action_model.py).
4. **Hand-to-mouth check** – MediaPipe Hands + FaceMesh
   ([`hand_face_detector.py`](hand_face_detector.py)) measure the minimum
   fingertip-to-mouth distance as a corroborating cue.
5. **Posture classification** – hip/knee/ankle geometry gives a
   standing/sitting/walking label independent of the action model.
6. **Temporal confirmation** – `update_smoking()` in [`main.py`](main.py)
   only confirms smoking when the smoke probability, repeated hand-to-mouth
   hits, and a multi-frame streak all hold; confirmed events (person id,
   start time, duration) are written to `smoking_events.csv` by
   [`event_logger.py`](event_logger.py).

## Files

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `main.py` | Full pipeline on a video file, writes an annotated MP4 |
| `camera main.py` | Same pipeline on a live webcam |
| `action_predictor.py` | Loads and runs the temporal action model |
| `pose_detector.py` | YOLOv8-pose keypoint extraction + track matching |
| `hand_face_detector.py` | MediaPipe hand-to-mouth distance |
| `prepare_action_data.py` | Builds pose sequences (`pose_action_data/`) from clips |
| `train_action_model.py` | Trains `action_model.keras` |
| `action_model.keras`, `action_scaler.pkl`, `action_labels.json` | Trained model + preprocessing |
| `models/smoking_model.pkl` | Earlier scikit-learn pose classifier |

## Setup

```bash
python -m venv .venv
.venv\Scripts\activate        # Windows
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

Requires Python 3.12. `yolov8n.pt` and `yolov8n-pose.pt` are included; the
first run of MediaPipe downloads its own model assets.

## Run

```bash
python main.py            # set VIDEO_SOURCE at the top of the file
python "camera main.py"   # webcam
```

Provide your own input video (large video files and the HMDB51 training
clips are not tracked in this repo).

## Retrain the action model

```bash
python prepare_action_data.py   # populate pose_action_data/<class>/*.npy
python train_action_model.py
```

## Notes

This is a research/educational prototype. Accuracy depends heavily on camera
angle, resolution, lighting and occlusion.
